==Dialogue==
[[File:SR-creature-Odahviing.jpg|thumb|Odahviing roaring]]
When shouting:
:''"{{hover|Inferno... Sun|Toor... Shul}}!"''

===The Fallen===
Immediately after his capture: 
:''"{{hover|No|Nid}}! {{hover|Trapped like a bear|Horvutah med kodaav}}. Caught like a bear in a trap... {{hover|My most eagerness (to) meet (you) in battle brought my defeat, Dragonborn|Zok frini grind ko grah drun viiki, Dovahkiin}}. Ah. I forget. You do not have the dovah speech. My... eagerness to meet you in battle was my... undoing, Dovahkiin. I salute your, hmm, low cunning in devising such a {{hover|stratagem|grahmindol}} - {{Sic|strategem|stratagem}}."''

Opening dialogue for the first time:
:''"{{hover|I am humbled|Zu'u bonaar}}. You went to a great deal of trouble to put me in this... humiliating position. {{hover|(You) wish to find Alduin|Hind siiv Alduin}}, hmm? No doubt you want to know where to find Alduin?"''
:'''That's right. Where is he hiding?'''
:''"{{hover|Very true.|Rinik vazah.}} An apt phrase. {{hover|Alduin fled (from you).|Alduin bovul.}} One reason I came to your call was to test your {{hover|Voice|Thu'um}} myself. Many of us have begun to question Alduin's lordship, whether his {{hover|Voice|Thu'um}} was truly the strongest. Among ourselves, of course. {{hover|We (are) not fools|Mu ni meyye}}. None were yet ready to openly defy him."''
:'''You were telling me where to find Alduin?'''
:''"{{hover|Unending sorrow|Unslaad krosis}}. Innumerable pardons. I digress. He has {{sic|travelled|traveled|description=British spelling}} to [[Skyrim:Sovngarde (place)|Sovngarde]] to regain his strength, devouring the {{hover|mortal souls|sillesejoor}}... the souls of the mortal dead. A privilege he jealously guards... His door to Sovngarde is at [[Skyrim:Skuldafn|Skuldafn]], one of his ancient fanes high in the eastern mountains. {{hover|As you know, all his dragon-loyalists (are) mustered there|Mindoraan, pah ok middovahhe lahvraan til.}} I surely do not need to warn you that all his remaining strength is {{sic|marshalled|marshaled|description=British spelling}} there. {{hover|I have given your want/request|Zu'u lost ofan hin laan}}... now that I have answered your question, you will allow me to go free?"''

You have two options, both of which lead to the same result.
:'''Do you promise to serve me?'''
::''"{{hover|Serve?|Aam?}} Serve you? ...no. {{hover|not time/not yet|Ni tiid.}} If and when you defeat Alduin, I will reconsider. Hmm... {{hover|Apologies|krosis}}. There is one detail about Skuldafn I neglected to mention."''
:'''Not until Alduin is defeated.'''
::''"Hmm... {{hover|Apologies|krosis}}. There is one detail about Skuldafn I neglected to mention."''
:'''Tell me what you know, then.'''
:''"Only this. You have the {{hover|Voice|Thu'um}} of a {{hover|dragon|dovah}}, but without the wings of one, you will never set foot in Skuldafn. Of course, I could fly you there. But not while imprisoned like this."''

===The World-Eater's Eyrie===
You have several options:
:'''We seem to be at an impasse, then.'''
::''"Indeed. {{hover|(a) fully beautiful balance|Orin brit ro}}. I cannot leave here until you defeat Alduin, which you cannot do without my help."''
:'''Do you expect me to take your word for that?'''
::''"{{hover|Wound|Ahraan}}. You wound me, Dovahkiin. I may not tell the whole truth, but I am no liar. Go and see for yourself. {{hover|I will be here|Zu'u ni bo nol het}}. I will be here... unless Alduin returns before you do."''
:'''Fine. I'll set you free if you promise to take me to Skuldafn.'''
:''"{{hover|Wisdom sees the one doorway|Onikaan koraav gein miraad.}} It is wise to recognize when you only have one choice. And you can trust me. {{hover|I'm not treacherous|Zu'u ni tahrodiis}}. Alduin has proven himself unworthy to rule. I go my own way now. Free me, and I will carry you to Skuldafn."''

If you speak to him again after exiting dialogue:
:''You will release me - {{hover|balanced request|ro laan}} - if in return I promise to take you to Skuldafn and stop helping Alduin?''
::'''I'm still wondering if I can trust you.'''
:::''"{{hover|I (am) not treacherous|Zu'u ni tahrodiis}}. It was you that lured me here and took me prisoner... {{hover|unworthy stratagem|vobalaan grahmindol}}. I have done nothing to earn your distrust."''
::::'''You did try to trick me into letting you go.'''
:::::''"{{hover|Your servant/slave, even now|Hin aar, orin nu}}. And yet here I am, still your prisoner."''
::::'''I guess I'll have to trust you.'''
:::::(Same response as below)
::'''Yes. I'll set you free if you promise to take me to Skuldafn.
:''"{{hover|Wisdom sees the one doorway|Onikaan koraav gein miraad.}} It is wise to recognize when you only have one choice. And you can trust me. {{hover|I'm not treacherous|Zu'u ni tahrodiis}}. Alduin has proven himself unworthy to rule. I go my own way now. Free me, and I will carry you to Skuldafn."''

Upon release:
:''"{{hover|Fear not, my honor holds my rage at bay.|Faas nu, zini dein ruthi ahst vaal}}."''

Speaking to him after he is released:
:''"{{hover|Await command|Saraan uth}} - I await your command, as promised. Are you ready to see the world as only a {{hover|dragon|dovah}} can?
::'''I'm ready. Take me to Skuldafn.'''
:::''"{{hover|Most beautiful command|Zok brit uth!}} I warn you, once you've flown the skies of {{hover|Skyrim|Keizaal}}, your envy of the {{hover|dragonkind|dov}} will only increase. {{hover|Onward! We fly into sky's freedom.|Amativ! Mu bo kotin stinselok.}}"''
::'''Hold on. I'm not quite ready.'''
:::''"{{hover|(You) bend my honor!|Kreh zini}}! The freedom of the sky beckons! Yet I stay here, {{hover|on earth|nau gol}}, as promised."''

Upon landing in Skuldafn:
:''"This is as far as I can take you. {{hover|Fight bravely|Krif voth ahkrin}}. I will look for your return, or Alduin's."''

===Dragonslayer===
After you've defeated Alduin and return to the [[Skyrim:Throat of the World|Throat of the World]], Odahviing will land and talk to you. His dialogue will differ if you chose to kill [[Skyrim:Paarthurnax (dragon)|Paarthurnax]] earlier.

{|class="hiddentable vtop"
|width=50%|<center>'''If Paarthurnax is alive:'''</center>
|width=50%|<center>'''If Paarthurnax is dead:'''</center>
|-
|
:''"{{hover|Good travels to the old one|Pruzah wundunne wah Wuth Gein}}. I wish the old one luck in his... quest. But I doubt many will wish to exchange Alduin's lordship for the tyranny of Paarthurnax's "Way of the Voice". As for myself, you've proven your mastery twice over. {{hover|(You are) my king/overlord, Dragonborn|Thuri, Dovahkiin}}. I gladly acknowledge the power of your Thu'um."''
|
:''"If Alduin himself could not stand against your Thu'um, I feel no shame in my own defeat. And so Alduin's lordship passes to you. {{hover|(You are) my king/overlord, Dragonborn|Thuri, Dovahkiin}}. I gladly submit to your mastery of the Thu'um."''
|}

Regardless, he will then tell you:
''"{{hover|I am Odahviing|Zu'u Odahviing}}. Call me when you have need, and I will come if I can."''

==Leveled List==

